WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:32.541
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna explained</b>

2
00:00:32.541 --> 00:00:36.416
<b>that an ignorant person </b>
<b>who lacks spiritual knowledge</b>

3
00:00:36.416 --> 00:00:42.000
<b>considers himself to be the </b>
<b>sole controller of his actions.</b>

4
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.958
<b>Such a person is filled with ego,</b>

5
00:00:44.958 --> 00:00:50.958
<b>constantly thinking that whatever</b>
<b>happens is a result of his doing. </b>

6
00:00:50.958 --> 00:00:55.625
<b>This type of person is considered </b>
<b>to be the most foolish.</b>

7
00:00:55.625 --> 00:00:56.458
<b>Now,</b>

8
00:00:56.458 --> 00:01:02.583
<b>in this verse, Lord Krishna is explaining </b>
<b>the mindset of a wise and enlightened person.</b>

9
00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:03.833
<b>He is describing</b>

10
00:01:03.833 --> 00:01:06.250
<b>the difference between an individual who </b>
<b>performs actions with attachment to the fruits </b>

11
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:12.041
<b>and one who acts selflessly with devotion.</b>

12
00:01:16.958 --> 00:01:18.166
<b>Lord Krishna</b>

13
00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:20.125
<b>tells Arjuna,</b>

14
00:01:20.125 --> 00:01:23.250
<b>A person attached to the fruits of their actions </b>

15
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:28.041
<b>and the one who acts selflessly with devotion.</b>

16
00:01:28.041 --> 00:01:31.625
<b>This difference in between them is of ‘Tattva-vit.’. </b>

17
00:01:31.625 --> 00:01:35.000
<b>'Tattva-vit' is the real knowledge of truth. </b>

18
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.041
<b>But what is this "Tattva-vit," </b>
<b>this knowledge of the truth?</b>

19
00:01:39.041 --> 00:01:44.625
<b>A wise person knows that </b>
<b>their true identity is the soul,</b>

20
00:01:44.625 --> 00:01:46.166
<b>not the body.</b>

21
00:01:46.166 --> 00:01:49.541
<b>They understand that the body, the senses,</b>

22
00:01:49.541 --> 00:01:54.375
<b>and the worldly experiences derived from </b>
<b>the senses' interaction with material objects </b>

23
00:01:54.375 --> 00:01:57.208
<b>are all aspects of the physical realm..</b>


24
00:01:57.208 --> 00:01:58.500
<b>For example,</b>

25
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:03.791
<b>they know that they are a </b>
<b>soul distinct from this body,</b>

26
00:02:03.791 --> 00:02:06.166
<b>distinct from the tongue of this body,</b>

27
00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:12.041
<b>and distinct from the sweetness that </b>
<b>the tongue experiences when tasting a sweet.</b>

28
00:02:12.041 --> 00:02:18.291
<b>They know that all of this is bound by the three </b>
<b>material qualities of tamas, rajas, and sattva.</b>

29
00:02:18.291 --> 00:02:21.916
<b>Tamas represents laziness and ignorance,</b>

30
00:02:21.916 --> 00:02:25.083
<b>rajas represents desires and struggle,</b>

31
00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:29.083
<b>and sattva represents peace and harmony.</b>

32
00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:32.250
<b>Every human being possesses these </b>
<b>three qualities in varying degrees,</b>

33
00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.750
<b>but these are all matters of the body.</b>

34
00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:39.791
<b>The house's external structure and </b>
<b>the appearance,</b>

35
00:02:39.791 --> 00:02:44.291
<b>are completely separate from the </b>
<b>person living inside it.</b>

36
00:02:44.291 --> 00:02:50.666
<b> the soul is merely residing </b>
<b>within this house-like body.</b>

37
00:02:50.666 --> 00:02:52.125
<b>Now, consider,</b>

38
00:02:52.125 --> 00:02:54.291
<b>what is more important?</b>

39
00:02:54.291 --> 00:02:55.916
<b>The appearance of the house?</b>

40
00:02:55.916 --> 00:02:58.458
<b>Or the person living inside?</b>

41
00:02:58.458 --> 00:03:02.000
<b>The goal of a wise person </b>
<b>is the upliftment of this soul.</b>

42
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.166
<b>They know that worrying </b>
<b>about this house-like body</b>

43
00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:10.916
<b>and being eager for its desires is futile.</b>

44
00:03:10.916 --> 00:03:11.916
<b>For this reason,</b>

45
00:03:11.916 --> 00:03:17.791
<b>they do not perform any action with </b>
<b>attachment to material desires.</b>

46
00:03:17.791 --> 00:03:22.458
<b>Such a wise person is far beyond attachments.</b>

47
00:03:26.125 --> 00:03:30.708
<b>There's a profound difference between </b>
<b>participating in life's activities merely as duties</b>

48
00:03:30.708 --> 00:03:34.458
<b>and becoming attached to their outcomes.</b>

49
00:03:34.458 --> 00:03:43.541
<b>This distinction fundamentally </b>
<b>shapes how we live our lives.</b>

50
00:03:43.541 --> 00:03:47.916
<b>Here, I am trying to explain to Arjuna</b>

51
00:03:47.916 --> 00:03:53.833
<b>the difference between one who participates </b>
<b>in life without attachment</b>

52
00:03:53.833 --> 00:04:00.125
<b>and one who lives constantly bound </b>
<b>by desires and attachments.</b>

53
00:04:00.125 --> 00:04:07.458
<b>How differently these two types of people live, </b>
<b>and what impact such lives create.</b>

54
00:04:07.458 --> 00:04:10.625
<b>Consider how tragic it is</b>

55
00:04:10.625 --> 00:04:15.416
<b> to live a life caught in an endless race –</b>

56
00:04:15.416 --> 00:04:20.416
<b>a race to accumulate more </b>
<b>and more material comforts,</b>

57
00:04:20.416 --> 00:04:26.833
<b>a competition to gain more wealth </b>
<b>and fame than others. </b>

58
00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:37.041
<b>This is tragic because such attachment, </b>
<b>such racing, is endless.</b>

59
00:04:37.041 --> 00:04:42.791
<b>The measure of such a life depends </b>
<b>not on you, but on others.</b>

60
00:04:42.791 --> 00:04:49.666
<b>It's like handing over the reins of your </b>
<b>happiness and contentment to someone else.</b>

61
00:04:49.666 --> 00:04:58.916
<b>If one lives such a comparative life, nothing but disappointment awaits.</b>

62
00:04:58.916 --> 00:05:06.166
<b>The right perspective on life is </b>
<b>to recognize one's true nature.</b>

63
00:05:06.166 --> 00:05:09.916
<b>To know that one is a soul,</b>

64
00:05:09.916 --> 00:05:18.166
<b>separate from this body, this material world,</b>
<b>and all its comforts.</b>

65
00:05:18.166 --> 00:05:21.791
<b>When one understands this true nature,</b>

66
00:05:21.791 --> 00:05:28.291
<b>they can rise above attachments </b>
<b>and live a purposeful life.</b>

67
00:05:28.291 --> 00:05:33.083
<b>Though participating in this material world, </b>
<b>they remain untouched by it.</b>

68
00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:37.458
<b>This perspective is liberating </b>
<b>in personal relationships too.</b>

69
00:05:37.458 --> 00:05:43.791
<b>You neither try to change yourself</b>
<b>to meet others' expectations,</b>

70
00:05:43.791 --> 00:05:50.541
<b>nor attempt to change others </b>
<b>to suit your preferences.</b>

71
00:05:50.541 --> 00:05:57.000
<b>Accepting others without trying to change them, </b>
<b>and accepting yourself as you are –</b>

72
00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:02.166
<b>this removes such a great</b>
<b>burden from relationships.</b>

73
00:06:02.166 --> 00:06:04.000
<b>Consider</b>

74
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:10.708
<b>how the inability to accept others as they are,</b>

75
00:06:10.708 --> 00:06:14.125
<b>the constant attempt to change them –</b>

76
00:06:14.125 --> 00:06:17.666
<b>isn't this the root cause of conflict </b>
<b>in personal relationships?</b>

77
00:06:17.666 --> 00:06:21.958
<b>One who knows the truth, </b>
<b>who has spiritual wisdom,</b>

78
00:06:21.958 --> 00:06:28.041
<b>sees in everyone the same soul as in themselves.</b>

79
00:06:28.041 --> 00:06:33.916
<b>Rising above their physical form, </b>
<b>nature, and behavior,</b>

80
00:06:33.916 --> 00:06:39.333
<b>they try to connect with others on a spiritual level.</b>

81
00:06:39.333 --> 00:06:45.750
<b>And this truth brings sweetness </b>
<b>to all their relationships.</b>

82
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:56.166
<b>What is one's true identity</b>
<b>in social and family settings?</b>

83
00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:58.625
<b>You must have noticed</b>

84
00:06:58.625 --> 00:07:04.750
<b>that whenever we meet others </b>
<b>at social or family gatherings,</b>

85
00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:10.750
<b>the conversation typically revolves around </b>
<b>who bought a new vehicle,</b>

86
00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:19.250
<b>who's going abroad for vacation, </b>
<b>who got promoted, and who fell behind.</b>

87
00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:24.333
<b>As if wealth, luxury, and position </b>
<b>alone define a person's identity.</b>

88
00:07:24.333 --> 00:07:27.250
<b>But is this the truth?</b>

89
00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:29.250
<b>No.</b>

90
00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:34.666
<b>None of these are under complete human control,</b>

91
00:07:34.666 --> 00:07:38.791
<b>nor have they been truly earned by oneself,</b>

92
00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:45.666
<b>nor will they accompany one after death.</b>

93
00:07:45.666 --> 00:07:51.208
<b>In this light, how hollow these matters appear.</b>

94
00:07:51.208 --> 00:07:52.708
<b>But</b>

95
00:07:52.708 --> 00:07:57.000
<b>if discussions centered </b>
<b>on life's meaningful aspects,</b>

96
00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.916
<b>this time would be so much better spent.</b>

97
00:08:00.916 --> 00:08:06.208
<b>Who is making spiritual and personal progress,</b>

98
00:08:06.208 --> 00:08:10.541
<b>who is striving to become a better human being,</b>

99
00:08:10.541 --> 00:08:14.750
<b>who is making a positive contribution to society,</b>

100
00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:17.250
<b>who is facing challenges,</b>

101
00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:19.583
<b>what new lessons are being learned,</b>

102
00:08:19.583 --> 00:08:25.125
<b>and if others in the group have </b>
<b>overcome similar challenges,</b>

103
00:08:25.125 --> 00:08:29.500
<b>they could share their experiences.</b>

104
00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:36.041
<b>This verse encourages us to understand </b>
<b>that while material achievements are necessary</b>

105
00:08:36.041 --> 00:08:40.000
<b>and form an important part of sustaining life,</b>

106
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:46.166
<b>these material accomplishments</b>
<b>are not one's true identity.</b>

107
00:08:46.166 --> 00:08:48.500
<b>True joy will come</b>

108
00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:56.583
<b>when we shift our social discussions </b>
<b>from materiality to spirituality.</b>

109
00:08:56.583 --> 00:09:06.250
<b>When this happens, we will respect others </b>
<b>for their nature, their soulfulness, their humanity –</b>

110
00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:09.333
<b>not for their wealth, property, and position.</b>

111
00:09:09.333 --> 00:09:13.375
<b>Instead of focusing on who's ahead </b>
<b>and who's behind in the race,</b>

112
00:09:13.375 --> 00:09:17.041
<b>discussions were based on spirituality,</b>

113
00:09:17.041 --> 00:09:19.791
<b>seeing everyone as equal,</b>

114
00:09:19.791 --> 00:09:24.750
<b>and maintaining a perspective </b>
<b>of mutual growth and support,</b>

115
00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:27.958
<b>how beautiful would the atmosphere be.</b>

116
00:09:27.958 --> 00:09:34.208
<b>You can certainly take the </b>
<b>first step in this direction.</b>

117
00:09:34.208 --> 00:09:36.000
<b>Think about it.</b>

118
00:09:40.541 --> 00:09:45.708
<b>Temptations at the workplace are quite natural.</b>

119
00:09:45.708 --> 00:09:47.708
<b>Sometimes there may be opportunities</b>

120
00:09:47.708 --> 00:09:51.958
<b>to earn more through improper means,</b>

121
00:09:51.958 --> 00:10:02.375
<b>or moments when one could advance by</b>
<b>hindering others' progress and pulling them down.</b>

122
00:10:02.375 --> 00:10:05.333
<b>What would you do in such situations?</b>

123
00:10:05.333 --> 00:10:08.625
<b>When one understands their truth,</b>

124
00:10:08.625 --> 00:10:14.708
<b>they neither find it difficult to follow ethics </b>
<b>during confusing times,</b>

125
00:10:14.708 --> 00:10:20.250
<b>nor face any dilemma in distinguishing </b>
<b>right from wrong.</b>

126
00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:21.958
<b>Imagine</b>

127
00:10:21.958 --> 00:10:27.041
<b>a person who knows their true worth.</b>

128
00:10:27.041 --> 00:10:33.666
<b>They understand that their real value </b>
<b>lies neither in position nor salary.</b>

129
00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:39.250
<b>Their true worth lies in their integrity, </b>
<b>in their ideals.</b>

130
00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:44.666
<b>Such a person will never stray </b>
<b>toward improper opportunities,</b>

131
00:10:44.666 --> 00:10:48.083
<b>neither chase wealth through corruption,</b>

132
00:10:48.083 --> 00:10:54.333
<b>nor use deceit to obstruct others' progress.</b>

133
00:10:54.333 --> 00:10:57.208
<b>Such a person knows</b>

134
00:10:57.208 --> 00:11:02.208
<b>that the benefits of corruption, deceit, </b>
<b>and fraud are temporary,</b>

135
00:11:02.208 --> 00:11:07.333
<b>but their negative impact lasts a lifetime.</b>

136
00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:12.916
<b>Tomorrow, positions may come and go, </b>
<b>salary may increase or decrease,</b>

137
00:11:12.916 --> 00:11:18.416
<b>but what remains constant is self-satisfaction,</b>

138
00:11:18.416 --> 00:11:22.416
<b>which only truth and ethics can provide.</b>

139
00:11:22.416 --> 00:11:26.208
<b>This ethics reflects in behavior too.</b>

140
00:11:26.208 --> 00:11:30.875
<b>An ethical person will always </b>
<b>respect their colleagues,</b>

141
00:11:30.875 --> 00:11:37.375
<b>viewing them equally regardless </b>
<b>of their position – higher or lower.</b>

142
00:11:37.375 --> 00:11:43.166
<b>Because they know that people's </b>
<b>true nature isn't their position.</b>

143
00:11:43.166 --> 00:11:48.791
<b>Just as a soul resides in a body for a limited time,</b>

144
00:11:48.791 --> 00:11:55.916
<b>similarly, a person holds </b>
<b>a position only temporarily.</b>

145
00:11:55.916 --> 00:12:00.375
<b>Just as the soul doesn't change </b>
<b>with the body's departure,</b>

146
00:12:00.375 --> 00:12:01.708
<b>similarly,</b>

147
00:12:01.708 --> 00:12:07.000
<b>a person's essence isn't tied to </b>
<b>having or not having a position.</b>

148
00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:11.208
<b>One who stays away from </b>
<b>deceit, fraud, and corruption –</b>

149
00:12:11.208 --> 00:12:14.416
<b>who respects everyone –</b>

150
00:12:14.416 --> 00:12:19.500
<b>naturally inspires us,</b>

151
00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:26.041
<b>and this is why such a person</b>
<b>is suitable for leadership.</b>

152
00:12:26.041 --> 00:12:31.750
<b>If you too wish to progress in life, </b>
<b>choose the path of ethics.</b>

153
00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:34.208
<b>Respect others.</b>

154
00:12:34.208 --> 00:12:36.000
<b>Your mind will remain peaceful,</b>

155
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.708
<b>and professional progress will follow.</b>

